// endpoint_subscribe_pull_request.proto — SubscribePullRequest: tell one
// workspace's agent about a GitHub pull request's comments, reviews, line
// comments, state changes and finished checks. AGENT API section.
//
// FOR PROGRAMS AND TESTS; AGENTS SUBSCRIBE BY OWNERSHIP. A workspace that
// stores a pull request it created as an OWNED link
// (ChangeWorkspaceLinksSet.ownership) is subscribed by the daemon, for every
// event, with no call of this rpc. This rpc takes the same subscription
// explicitly (PullRequestSubscriptionOriginRequested).
//
// DELIVERY. Each notice (PullRequestNotice) is submitted to the subscriber's
// session as a deferred prompt of origin
// conversation.v1.PromptOrigin.PROMPT_ORIGIN_PULL_REQUEST_NOTICE: it waits
// behind a running turn, wakes an idle agent, and the feed draws no row for
// it. How the daemon reads GitHub, and why nothing can be lost or told twice,
// is pull_request.proto's header.
//
// NOTHING SLIPS BETWEEN READING AND FOLLOWING. The answer carries the pull
// request as it stands when the subscription is taken, and every piece of
// activity after that read is told.
//
// SCOPE AND LIFETIME. A subscriber holds at most one subscription per pull
// request; subscribing again replaces its events and keeps what it was
// already told. A subscription ends when the pull request merges or closes
// (after the notice saying so), when the subscriber unsubscribes, and when the
// subscriber closes however it closes. It is DURABLE across a daemon restart
// and a handover.

